  "limitations": [
    "Cold subprocess timings may hit the OS file-system cache from this same benchmark run's earlier fixture writes/reads; not a true cold-disk measurement.",
    "QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen is used throughout; WebEngine numbers reflect local setHtml() navigation on a headless surface, not a real on-screen first paint -- needs a manual Windows check.",
    "body_render_ms conflates markdown-it parsing and Pygments/anchor HTML generation because app/md_converter.py has no internal stage boundary between them (see ConverterInstrumentation docstring).",
    "This tool never imports app.renderer's QThreadPool worker directly to avoid depending on GUI wiring under change; GUI heartbeat/contention tests reproduce the same shared _CONVERT_LOCK usage pattern instead.",
    "Stress categories (code_heavy/big_table/math_mermaid/long_paragraph) were measured in a separate invocation with reduced warm-reopen reps (3, vs 10 for long_prose) and no GUI/WebEngine/contention/memory passes, to keep the wall-clock time for this delivery bounded; code_heavy in particular is slow (~36s/5MB, ~90s/10MB) because markdown_it + Pygments is called once per code fence and the generator packs many fences into one document."
